01:02:51,428 --> 01:02:57,428
Michael Collins is a 1996 biographical historical drama film about Michael Collins, a leading figure
in the early-20th-century Irish struggle for independence against the United Kingdom.

11
01:09:08,571 --> 01:09:14,571
It is written and directed by Neil Jordan and stars Liam Neeson in the title role,
along with Aidan Quinn, Stephen Rea, Alan Rickman, and Julia Roberts.

12
01:15:25,714 --> 01:15:31,714
The film was distributed by Warner Bros.

13
01:21:42,857 --> 01:21:48,857
An international co-production between Ireland, the United States, and the United Kingdom,
Michael Collins was one of the most expensive films ever produced in Ireland.

14
01:28:00,000 --> 01:28:06,000
Filming took place in Dublin, and the score was composed by Elliot Goldenthal.

15
01:34:17,142 --> 01:34:23,142
Michael Collins won the Golden Lion at the 53rd Venice International
Film Festival, with Neeson winning the Best Actor Award.

16
01:40:34,285 --> 01:40:40,285
It received a limited release in the United States on 11 October
1996, before going to a wide release on 25 October.

17
01:46:51,428 --> 01:46:57,428
It was released in Ireland on 8 November.

18
01:53:08,571 --> 01:53:14,571
It received generally positive reviews, and was nominated for Best Original
Score and Best Cinematography at the 69th Academy Awards.

19
01:59:25,714 --> 01:59:31,714
The film explores themes of civil war, fight,
presidential election, freedom fighter, biography.

20
02:05:42,857 --> 02:05:48,857
